WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.350
Here's what those records leave to
you, and each row is pinned by a test.

2
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:08.556
The disable and the session update
are separate records, and a disabled

3
00:00:08.556 --> 00:00:12.975
account with live sessions isn't blocked,
so the block is the later of the two.

4
00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:17.262
A run's completion says the workflow
finished, not when access stopped.

5
00:00:17.262 --> 00:00:21.799
The catch-up window is only prose,
so a late entry gets its own rule.

6
00:00:21.799 --> 00:00:26.462
A failed disable sits in the same log,
so only successful records count.

7
00:00:26.462 --> 00:00:30.140
And a failed task, or a
re-enable, each gets a rule.
